WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.570
Got a lot of links to download at once?

2
00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:05.602
Open the Batch tab in the New download window.

3
00:00:05.602 --> 00:00:07.183
Paste one link per line.

4
00:00:07.183 --> 00:00:11.862
Make sure each link is on its own line so it's read as a separate item.

5
00:00:11.862 --> 00:00:14.432
Arus accepts up to fifty links at once.

6
00:00:14.432 --> 00:00:19.704
Each one becomes its own download, with the same folder and connection settings.

7
00:00:19.704 --> 00:00:23.856
You can set priority or a speed cap after they're in the queue.

8
00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:27.283
For video on a web page, switch to the Web page tab.

9
00:00:27.283 --> 00:00:29.919
Paste the page address, then click Scan.

10
00:00:29.919 --> 00:00:34.730
Arus reads the page and lists the video, audio, and HLS sources it finds.

11
00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:36.378
Pick the source you need.

12
00:00:36.378 --> 00:00:39.607
Arus downloads it as a file that's ready to play.

13
00:00:39.607 --> 00:00:43.627
Once added, every item can be managed like a normal download.

14
00:00:43.627 --> 00:00:48.174
Batch and Scan turn a job full of clicks into a much faster workflow.

15
00:00:48.174 --> 00:00:52.062
It's handy for study materials, archives, or project files.

